  "layout_note": "COMPLETE Matthew ch.28 (resurrection) on one page: running header; 'CHAP. XXVIII.' heading; italic Argument (5 lines, real cursive w); single wide text column opened by a woodcut floriated drop-cap 'A'; left-margin roman scripture cross-refs; right-margin roman liturgical rubrics ('The Ghoſpel for...'); 'ANNO-' catchword foot-right (the ANNOTATIONS follow on p103). Body vv.1-20 complete; v20 ends '...conſummation of the world.'. Roman BODY uses a REAL 'w' cut in vv-style (same regime as 2 John in this NT-1582 volume); the italic Argument sets a REAL cursive w. Digitization marks excluded (red papal-keys shield bottom-left; www.fatimamovement.com watermark). NOTE this page CORRECTS a prior mislocation: the sibling files scripture-matthew-28-p103/104/105 are NOT Mt28 body (they are, respectively, the Mt28 ANNOTATIONS, the Argument of S. Mark, and a St Mark engraving plate).",
  "chapter_heading": "CHAP. XXVIII.",
  "argument": {
    "role": "argument",
    "typeface": "italic",
    "text": "He riſeth againe the third day , & ( the blind moſt obſtinate Iewes by bribery working to their owne reprobation ) he appeareth to his Diſciples in Galilee ( as both before his Paſſion he foretold them Mat. 26. and now after his Reſurrection.firſt the Angel, then alſo himſelf appointed by the women ) 18. and ſendeth them to al Nations, to build his Church among the Gentils.",
    "note": "italic face uses REAL cursive w (working, now, women); embedded ref 'Mat. 26.'"
  },
